  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For the neutralization between a strong and a strong base, equal number of moles of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> (from acid) and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mo>̄</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> (from base) come out. For one mole of each following equation can be drawn<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/686b725a-e60c-4316-8e10-8704d053b5ca.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.38333in;height:1.025in\" /><br />So, 0.35 mole of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is produced.<br />So, heat released <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0.35</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>13.7</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.795</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>",
